  "synthesis": "The topic label centers on immune spatial transcriptomics, but the listed items mostly address adjacent methods rather than immune-specific spatial analyses. DeSPA detects genes with cross-state spatial pattern remodeling across replicate slices and groups them into spatial programs. SORT recovers multilevel gene programs from spatial atlases, validated on PDAC. Related single-cell work includes HyperCom for hypergraph-based cell-cell communication inference, NetMap for joint regulatory network inference and cell clustering, and DECONVersation for bulk RNA-seq deconvolution using foundation model embeddings. Most activity is in preprints, with three peer-reviewed items. No code releases or industry signals are recorded, and the 7-day star gain is zero. The observed rise reflects item volume only; the items do not establish drivers.",
